cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Citation is not required. If this software was useful for your teaching or research,
  you are welcome to cite it as below.
title: "SymVib"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ishii
    given-names: Yosuke
    affiliation: Nagoya Institute of Technology
version: 2.2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24085930
license-url: "https://github.com/youskeishii141-yi/symvib/blob/main/LICENSE"  # MIT + Commons Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/youskeishii141-yi/symvib"
abstract: >-
  Python tools (GUI and command line) that assign the vibrational modes of isolated molecules
  (45 point groups) and crystals (Γ-point factor-group analysis for all 230 space groups) to
  irreducible representations, determine their IR/Raman activity and Raman tensor forms, and
  write the displacement patterns for visualization in VESTA. Directions fixed by symmetry are
  distinguished from those that need force constants (estimated with a spring-network model, or
  obtained from Quantum ESPRESSO forces with the frozen-phonon tool).
keywords:
  - group theory
  - vibrational spectroscopy
  - Raman
  - infrared
  - factor group analysis
  - phonon
  - education
